WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:17.694
Edward walked away from the palace, people continued to laugh whenever he called himself a prince.

2
00:00:19.095 --> 00:00:23.337
He continued to shout at them for not recognizing him as the heir to the throne.

3
00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:27.500
At last everyone got bored and ignored him.

4
00:00:31.892 --> 00:00:35.994
By this time Edward's feet were sore, so he stopped to bathe them in a creek.

5
00:00:38.456 --> 00:00:41.177
Looking around, he recognized a nearby building.

6
00:00:42.558 --> 00:00:46.080
His father had turned it into a home for poor, abandoned children.

7
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:51.263
"My father has been generous to the children," Edward thought.

8
00:00:51.283 --> 00:00:54.244
"So I'll be treated kindly there."

9
00:00:55.545 --> 00:00:59.727
He looked down at his ragged clothes, which belonged to Tom, and sighed.

10
00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:05.095
"Right now I'm as poor as the children who live there."

11
00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:11.000
Edward spotted a group of boys playing in a courtyard.

12
00:01:12.101 --> 00:01:14.463
They were all dressed alike in the school's uniform.

13
00:01:15.864 --> 00:01:20.568
The boys quickly gathered around Edward, who misinterpreted this as a sign of respect.

14
00:01:20.588 --> 00:01:28.875
"Good lads," he said, "please tell whoever is in charge of this home that Prince Edward wishes to

15
00:01:28.935 --> 00:01:29.556
speak to him."

16
00:01:35.112 --> 00:01:39.094
A loud shout went up, and the boys laughed at this stranger in rags.

17
00:01:39.114 --> 00:01:42.716
"And who are you, beggar?"

18
00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.598
asked one boy, who seemed to be their leader.

19
00:01:45.618 --> 00:01:48.219
"The prince's messenger?"

20
00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:52.341
"I am the prince!

21
00:01:52.922 --> 00:01:54.923
How dare you speak to me that way!"

22
00:01:55.963 --> 00:02:00.386
Edward was outraged because he was used to being obeyed, not insulted.

23
00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:04.628
His hand flew to his hip, but he found nothing there.

24
00:02:07.692 --> 00:02:08.653
"Did you see that?"

25
00:02:08.993 --> 00:02:09.974
another boy asked.

26
00:02:09.994 --> 00:02:13.717
"He thought he had a sword just like a real prince!"

27
00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:19.241
The boys laughed again.

28
00:02:20.281 --> 00:02:21.362
Edward stood up tall.

29
00:02:21.382 --> 00:02:26.826
"You should be grateful that my father, the king, provides you with food and clothing.

30
00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.408
And you shouldn't be rude to me."

31
00:02:36.056 --> 00:02:38.197
This made the boys laugh even louder.

32
00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:43.538
"You are correct, Your Royal Highness," the first boy said.

33
00:02:43.558 --> 00:02:46.859
"Down on your knees, loyal subjects!"

34
00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.921
Snickering and poking each other, the boys dropped to their knees and bowed their heads.

35
00:02:54.421 --> 00:02:57.622
Tired of being mocked, Edward kicked at the nearest boy.

36
00:02:57.642 --> 00:02:58.902
"Take that!"

37
00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:00.443
he cried as he missed.

38
00:03:02.523 --> 00:03:04.764
The group's mood instantly changed to anger.

39
00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:06.901
"Throw him in the creek!"

40
00:03:07.421 --> 00:03:08.321
someone called out.

41
00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.603
For a moment Edward was stunned.

42
00:03:13.663 --> 00:03:15.724
These boys were going to toss him in the water!

43
00:03:16.805 --> 00:03:19.005
Then he turned and ran as fast as he could.

44
00:03:20.246 --> 00:03:22.647
He didn't dare look back until he was far away.

45
00:03:24.328 --> 00:03:27.089
When he did, the boys were nowhere to be seen.

46
00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:31.891
"It's a good thing I'm a fast runner."

47
00:03:32.871 --> 00:03:34.752
Edward smiled in spite of himself.

48
00:03:35.864 --> 00:03:38.645
"I could probably beat Tom Canty and his friends."

49
00:03:41.806 --> 00:03:45.987
For the rest of the day, Edward wandered the streets, looking for Tom's house.

50
00:03:46.007 --> 00:03:52.909
"If I can find Offal Street, Tom's family will realize that I'm the prince," he thought.

51
00:03:52.929 --> 00:03:56.830
"And they'll immediately take me back to the palace."

52
00:04:00.151 --> 00:04:03.152
But as night fell, Edward was still out on the streets.

53
00:04:04.512 --> 00:04:07.554
He grew so tired and hungry that he could barely walk.

54
00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:13.398
He gave up asking for directions because everyone insulted him instead of helping him.

55
00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:21.444
After a while he stopped being angry with the boys at the children's home.

56
00:04:21.464 --> 00:04:26.627
"Food and clothing are important, but they're not enough," he thought.

57
00:04:26.647 --> 00:04:31.370
"When I'm king, those boys will have an education too.

58
00:04:32.671 --> 00:04:35.085
And hopefully, they'll learn to be kind."

59
00:04:37.485 --> 00:04:41.047
Edward pressed on as it began to rain and the wind picked up.

60
00:04:42.948 --> 00:04:46.689
He drifted deeper into the maze of filthy streets where the poor lived.

61
00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:51.091
Suddenly a man grabbed Edward by the back of his neck.

62
00:04:51.111 --> 00:04:52.732
"Got you!"

63
00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:53.672
he cried.

64
00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:58.394
"Out at this time of night, and I bet you don't have a penny to bring home.

65
00:04:59.794 --> 00:05:04.688
If that's not true, then my name's not John Canty, and I'll—" "John Canty?"

66
00:05:06.109 --> 00:05:08.409
Edward twisted around to see the man's face.

67
00:05:08.429 --> 00:05:11.010
"Are you really John Canty?

68
00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.070
Then you must be his father!

69
00:05:14.151 --> 00:05:15.891
Take me back to the palace immediately."

70
00:05:15.911 --> 00:05:18.392
"His father?

71
00:05:18.752 --> 00:05:19.432
The palace?

72
00:05:20.733 --> 00:05:22.173
I don't know what you're talking about.

73
00:05:23.113 --> 00:05:28.915
But I do know that I'm your father, and you'll soon regret—" "I can't stand this a minute

74
00:05:28.995 --> 00:05:30.515
longer!" Edward cried.

75
00:05:30.535 --> 00:05:36.290
"Take me back to my father, King Henry, and he'll make you rich beyond your wildest dreams.

76
00:05:37.691 --> 00:05:39.713
Believe me, I'm telling the truth.

77
00:05:41.154 --> 00:05:43.716
I am Prince Edward, the heir to the throne.

78
00:05:44.837 --> 00:05:45.958
I'm not Tom!"

79
00:05:49.141 --> 00:05:51.362
Confused, John stared at the boy.

80
00:05:51.382 --> 00:05:56.607
"I don't know what game you're playing, or if there's something wrong with your mind.

81
00:05:57.588 --> 00:05:59.729
But you're going home with me to Offal Street."

82
00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.612
He grabbed Edward again.

83
00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:05.041
"Help me!"

84
00:06:05.462 --> 00:06:08.065
Edward cried as people passed by.

85
00:06:08.806 --> 00:06:13.191
But John was already dragging the frantic, struggling boy toward Offal Street.

86
00:06:16.155 --> 00:06:20.360
A few curious onlookers followed them, but no one tried to help poor Edward.
